    "srt_text": "1\n00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,282\nWelcome back to Strange Nature.\n\n2\n00:00:02,282 --> 00:00:05,080\nI'm your host, and today, the octopus.\n\n3\n00:00:05,080 --> 00:00:12,380\nAn octopus has three hearts: two pump blood through the gills, and one drives it around the body.\n\n4\n00:00:12,380 --> 00:00:17,180\nThat blood runs blue because it carries oxygen with copper instead of iron.\n\n5\n00:00:17,180 --> 00:00:28,140\nOf its roughly 500 million neurons, nearly two-thirds live not in its head, but in its arms.\n\n6\n00:00:28,140 --> 00:00:31,420\nEach arm tastes, touches, and partly decides on its own.\n\n7\n00:00:31,420 --> 00:00:33,292\nAnd here's the strangest part.\n\n8\n00:00:33,292 --> 00:00:45,020\nAn octopus is functionally colorblind, yet it can match the color and texture of coral, sand, or stone in under a second using thousands of pigment cells in its skin called chromatophores.\n\n9\n00:00:45,020 --> 00:00:53,478\nSome scientists call it the closest thing we have to alien intelligence.\n\n10\n00:00:53,478 --> 00:00:59,000\nMaybe intelligence doesn't need a spine at all.\n"
